Subject: [PATCH 31/31] =?UTF-8?q?Plutonium:=20the=20dock:=20Super+1?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=A69=20slots=20for=20the=20terminal,=20apps=20and=20sites?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Nine slots, each T3's terminal drawer, an app or a site, kept in this
thread, this project or everywhere (a Plutonium tag: t3:thread/<id>,
t3:project/<id>, t3:global). Super+N starts what the slot names, shows it,
gives it the keyboard, and goes back to where you were on the next press;
several copies cycle. A slot is split (beside the chat) or fold (the chat
folds away: the panel's maximize, or the terminal drawer taking the column);
Super+Ctrl+N the other way this time, Super+Up switches it for the thread.
Super+Shift+N, or a panel tab's menu, puts something in a slot. Slot 1 is
the terminal by default. The keys only apply in the Plutonium shell.

A focused tab's page or app window no longer loses the keyboard to the
composer when the shell window's focus event follows (EMBED, NATIVE-WINDOW).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
